</div></div></div><div id=3D"section/First-steps" data-section-id=3D"sectio=
n/First-steps" class=3D"sc-eCIkAO eLcbNt"><div class=3D"sc-iCfNyT gBxmSK"><=
div class=3D"sc-hKwBjT knScuR"><h1 class=3D"sc-imWYAI crttPH"><a class=3D"s=
c-jlZhew jrsfjb" href=3D"https://docs.bexio.com/#section/First-steps" aria-=
label=3D"section/First-steps"></a>First steps</h1></div></div><div class=3D=
"sc-hKwBjT gOILhW"><div class=3D"sc-iJKPHa sc-cCcVtu cJMweq cwfHHQ redoc-ma=
rkdown " html=3D"&lt;p&gt;In order to use the bexio API, you need to follow=
 the following steps in order:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create a bexio account by signing up for a trial account at &lt;a=
 href=3D&quot;https://www.bexio.com&quot;&gt;https://www.bexio.com&lt;/a&gt=
; and complete the onboarding process.
If you already have a bexio account, you can skip this step.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Go to the developer portal at &lt;a href=3D&quot;https://develope=
r.bexio.com&quot;&gt;https://developer.bexio.com&lt;/a&gt; and log in using=
 your bexio credentials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Read and accept the &lt;a href=3D&quot;https://cdn.www.bexio.com/=
assets/content/documents/legal/bexio_marketplace_agb_EN.pdf&quot;&gt;terms =
and conditions&lt;/a&gt; (please pay special attention to the commercial us=
e regulations mentioned in Section 4.4).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create a new app and make sure that you define a valid site for t=
he &amp;quot;Allowed redirect URL&amp;quot; field(s)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;By clicking on the section &amp;quot;App Details&amp;quot; you ca=
n reveal the Client ID and Client Secret&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Initiate the &lt;a href=3D&quot;#section/Authentication/Authoriza=
tion-Code-Flow&quot;&gt;Authorization Code Flow&lt;/a&gt; to obtain an acce=
ss token.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use the access token to create a request to the bexio API. The ex=
ample below fetches a list of contacts (make sure to request the scope &lt;=
code&gt;contact_show&lt;/code&gt; in the authorization code flow)&lt;/li&gt=
;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;curl &lt;span class=3D&quot;token operator&quot;&gt;=
-&lt;/span&gt;X GET \
      https&lt;span class=3D&quot;token punctuation&quot;&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;=
&lt;span class=3D&quot;token operator&quot;&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=
=3D&quot;token operator&quot;&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;api&lt;span class=3D&quot;to=
ken punctuation&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;bexio&lt;span class=3D&quot;token pu=
nctuation&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;com&lt;span class=3D&quot;token operator&q=
uot;&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=3D&quot;token number&quot;&gt;2.0&lt;/=
span&gt;&lt;span class=3D&quot;token operator&quot;&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;contac=
t \
      &lt;span class=3D&quot;token operator&quot;&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;H &lt;sp=
an class=3D&quot;token string&quot;&gt;'Accept: application/json'&lt;/span&=
gt; \
      &lt;span class=3D&quot;token operator&quot;&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;H &lt;sp=
an class=3D&quot;token string&quot;&gt;'Authorization: Bearer {access-token=
}'&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Make sure to replace &lt;code&gt;{access-token}&lt;/code&gt; with =
the token you received in Step 6.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
"><p>In order to use the bexio API, you need to follow the following steps =
in order:</p>
<ol>
<li>Create a bexio account by signing up for a trial account at <a href=3D"=
https://www.bexio.com/">https://www.bexio.com</a> and complete the onboardi=
ng process.
If you already have a bexio account, you can skip this step.</li>
<li>Go to the developer portal at <a href=3D"https://developer.bexio.com/">=
https://developer.bexio.com</a> and log in using your bexio credentials.</l=
i>
<li>Read and accept the <a href=3D"https://cdn.www.bexio.com/assets/content=
/documents/legal/bexio_marketplace_agb_EN.pdf">terms and conditions</a> (pl=
ease pay special attention to the commercial use regulations mentioned in S=
ection 4.4).</li>
<li>Create a new app and make sure that you define a valid site for the "Al=
lowed redirect URL" field(s)</li>
<li>By clicking on the section "App Details" you can reveal the Client ID a=
nd Client Secret</li>
<li>Initiate the <a href=3D"https://docs.bexio.com/#section/Authentication/=
Authorization-Code-Flow">Authorization Code Flow</a> to obtain an access to=
ken.</li>
<li>Use the access token to create a request to the bexio API. The example =
below fetches a list of contacts (make sure to request the scope <code>cont=
act_show</code> in the authorization code flow)</li>
</ol>
<pre><code>curl <span class=3D"token operator">-</span>X GET \
      https<span class=3D"token punctuation">:</span><span class=3D"token o=
perator">/</span><span class=3D"token operator">/</span>api<span class=3D"t=
oken punctuation">.</span>bexio<span class=3D"token punctuation">.</span>co=
m<span class=3D"token operator">/</span><span class=3D"token number">2.0</s=
pan><span class=3D"token operator">/</span>contact \
      <span class=3D"token operator">-</span>H <span class=3D"token string"=
>'Accept: application/json'</span> \
      <span class=3D"token operator">-</span>H <span class=3D"token string"=
>'Authorization: Bearer {access-token}'</span>
</code></pre>
<blockquote>
<p>Make sure to replace <code>{access-token}</code> with the token you rece=
ived in Step 6.</p>
</blockquote>
