&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The user clicks Login within the regular web application.&lt;/li&=
gt;
&lt;li&gt;The web application redirects the user to the &lt;code&gt;/author=
ize&lt;/code&gt; endpoint of the bexio OpenID Connect service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The bexio OpenID Connect Service displays the login page.&lt;/li&=
gt;
&lt;li&gt;The user authenticates and sees a consent page listing the permis=
sions bexio will give to the web application.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The user is redirected back to the web application with an Author=
ization Code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The web application sends this code to the bexio OpenID Connect s=
ervice (&lt;code&gt;/token&lt;/code&gt; endpoint) along with the applicatio=
n&amp;#39;s Client ID and Client Secret.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;bexio verifies the code, Client ID, and Client Secret.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ID Token and Access Token (and optionally, a Refresh Token) is=
 returned to the web application.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The web application uses the Access Token to call the bexio API.&=
lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The bexio API responds with requested data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
