<ol>
<li>The user clicks Login within the regular web application.</li>
<li>The web application redirects the user to the <code>/authorize</code> e=
ndpoint of the bexio OpenID Connect service.</li>
<li>The bexio OpenID Connect Service displays the login page.</li>
<li>The user authenticates and sees a consent page listing the permissions =
bexio will give to the web application.</li>
<li>The user is redirected back to the web application with an Authorizatio=
n Code.</li>
<li>The web application sends this code to the bexio OpenID Connect service=
 (<code>/token</code> endpoint) along with the application's Client ID and =
Client Secret.</li>
<li>bexio verifies the code, Client ID, and Client Secret.</li>
<li>An ID Token and Access Token (and optionally, a Refresh Token) is retur=
ned to the web application.</li>
<li>The web application uses the Access Token to call the bexio API.</li>
<li>The bexio API responds with requested data.</li>
</ol>
<h3 id=3D"code-example-php">Code example (PHP)</h3>
