&lt;p&gt;The scope &lt;code&gt;offline_access&lt;/code&gt; is required to o=
btain a refresh token to keep the api connection alive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;POST a request to the endpoint =E2=80=9C/token=E2=80=9D. Make sur=
e you use the grant type =E2=80=9Crefresh_token=E2=80=9D. This is implement=
ed according to the standards of &lt;a href=3D&quot; https://tools.ietf.org=
/html/rfc6749#section-1.5&quot; &gt; OAuth 2.0 RFC 6749 &lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&g=
t;
&lt;li&gt;The response contains a new access token. Please note that the re=
quested scopes do not change when refreshing a token. Acquiring new scopes =
is only possible by going through the initial authorization process again.&=
lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The new access token can be used to authorize requests and execut=
e API requests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The bexio API responds with the requested data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
