n/API-basics/HTTP-Verbs" aria-label=3D"section/API-basics/HTTP-Verbs"></a>H=
TTP Verbs</h2></div></div><div class=3D"sc-hKwBjT gOILhW"><div class=3D"sc-=
iJKPHa sc-cCcVtu cJMweq cwfHHQ redoc-markdown " html=3D"&lt;p&gt;Where poss=
ible, bexio tries to use the appropriate HTTP verb for its operations&lt;/p=
&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Verb&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Description&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;GET&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Used for retrieving resources&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;POST&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Used for creating resources&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;PATCH&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Used for updating resources with partial data&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;PUT&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Used for updating resources with full data&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;DELETE&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Used for deleting resources. Please note that delete actions perm=
anently delete resources. It cannot be undone.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
"><p>Where possible, bexio tries to use the appropriate HTTP verb for its o=
perations</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Verb</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody><tr>
<td><code>GET</code></td>
<td>Used for retrieving resources</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>POST</code></td>
<td>Used for creating resources</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>PATCH</code></td>
<td>Used for updating resources with partial data</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>PUT</code></td>
<td>Used for updating resources with full data</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>DELETE</code></td>
<td>Used for deleting resources. Please note that delete actions permanentl=
y delete resources. It cannot be undone.</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
</div></div></div><div id=3D"section/API-basics/HTTP-Headers" data-section-=
id=3D"section/API-basics/HTTP-Headers" class=3D"sc-eCIkAO eLcbNt"><div clas=
s=3D"sc-iCfNyT gBxmSK"><div class=3D"sc-hKwBjT knScuR"><h2 class=3D"sc-jrQA=
on esUxnh"><a class=3D"sc-crHjOq bVILEW" href=3D"https://docs.bexio.com/#se=
ction/API-basics/HTTP-Headers" aria-label=3D"section/API-basics/HTTP-Header=
s"></a>HTTP Headers</h2></div></div><div class=3D"sc-hKwBjT gOILhW"><div cl=
ass=3D"sc-iJKPHa sc-cCcVtu cJMweq cwfHHQ redoc-markdown " html=3D"&lt;p&gt;=
HTTP headers let the client and the server pass additional information with=
 an HTTP request or response.
An HTTP header consists of its case-insensitive name followed by a colon (:=
), then by its value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=3D&quot;request-headers&quot;&gt;Request Headers&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The following headers must be used for every request:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;Accept: application/json&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;Authorization: Bearer &amp;lt;token&amp;gt;&lt;/code&=
gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Additionally, the header &lt;code&gt;Content-Length: &amp;lt;lengt=
h&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; must be specified for requests with a payload.&lt;/p=
&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;Accept-Language: xx&lt;/code&gt; can be used to sp=
ecify the language you would like to have some translated elements returned=
 to you. The &lt;code&gt;xx&lt;/code&gt; has to be replaced by the ISO 639-=
1 code of the language. This is for example useful to have the tax codes in=
 the user=E2=80=99s language.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=3D&quot;response-headers&quot;&gt;Response Headers&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The API will always indicate the return type with a &lt;code&gt;Co=
ntent-Type&lt;/code&gt; header.
Normally the header value is set to &lt;code&gt;application/json&lt;/code&g=
t;, but can vary (e.g. for PDF exports).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Response Codes
Actions and errors yield different HTTP response codes. Please have a look =
at the expected response codes in the following list:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Code&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Description&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;200&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Request OK&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;201&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;New resource created&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;304&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The resource has not been changed&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;400&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The request parameters are invalid&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;401&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The bearer token or the provided api key is invalid&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;403&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;You do not possess the required rights to access this resource&lt=
;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;404&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The resource could not be found / is unknown&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;411&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Length Required&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;415&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The data could not be processed or the accept header is invalid&l=
t;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;422&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Could not save the entity&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;429&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Too many requests&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;500&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;An unexpected condition was encountered&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;503&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The server is not available (maintenance work)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
"><p>HTTP headers let the client and the server pass additional information=
 with an HTTP request or response.
An HTTP header consists of its case-insensitive name followed by a colon (:=
), then by its value.</p>
<h3 id=3D"request-headers">Request Headers</h3>
<p>The following headers must be used for every request:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>Accept: application/json</code></li>
<li><code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;</code></li>
</ul>
<p>Additionally, the header <code>Content-Length: &lt;length&gt;</code> mus=
t be specified for requests with a payload.</p>
<p>The <code>Accept-Language: xx</code> can be used to specify the language=
 you would like to have some translated elements returned to you. The <code=
>xx</code> has to be replaced by the ISO 639-1 code of the language. This i=
s for example useful to have the tax codes in the user=E2=80=99s language.<=
/p>
<h3 id=3D"response-headers">Response Headers</h3>
<p>The API will always indicate the return type with a <code>Content-Type</=
code> header.
Normally the header value is set to <code>application/json</code>, but can =
